## Worksheet

**F1 – Core loop:** Game class holds state; mulberry32 seeds rng; endTurn() has fixed step order — BUT triggerAshstorm() uses raw `Math.random()` instead of `this.rng()`, breaking "seeded PRNG for all randomness." Score 1.

**F2 – Map:** 64-tile grid, generateTerrain() uses this.rng(); isValidBuild() checks building.terrain; adjBonus multiplies output in produceResources(). Score 2.

**F3 – Economy:** forge consumes ore→metal, greenhouse consumes water→food; caps enforced via Math.min(..., caps[r]); BUT consume never gates production — output always produced even with 0 input stock. Score 1.

**F4 – Population:** generateColonist() sets skill/fatigue/morale; buildingAssignments arrays exist but nothing ever pushes colonists into them, so skill/fatigue never actually affect production; person.job never set. Score 1.

**F5 – Needs:** food/water decremented per colonist; shortage sets morale -=30 in endTurn(); recovery (+5/turn) exists; BUT morale is never read in produceResources() — no output effect. Score 1.

**F6 – Research:** 12 nodes, prereq check + spend() in research_upgrade(); soil_enrichment/water_capture/metallurgy/ore_extraction/specialization/reinforced_walls/storm_shelter all read in produceResources/triggerAshstorm; but renewable_power, biotech, energy_storage, advanced_trading have zero call sites anywhere. Score 1.

**F7 – Events:** exactly 10 in EVENTS_DECK; fireRandomEvent() selection is uniform (`rng()*available.length`), not weighted; 9 events have 2-3 choices with distinct effect() mutations; eventCooldown gates re-firing. Score 1.

**F8 – Trade:** buyTrade/sellTrade wired to buttons, qty gated on buy; price = basePrice * random * tradeMultiplier — never reads player resources/stockpiles, tradeMultiplier only from one event then resets. Score 1.

**F9 – Hazard:** triggerAshstorm() scales severity with turn, mitigated by reinforced_walls/storm_shelter/wall+shelter count; but damage = outright building deletion (`buildings[i]=null`), no partial-damage state or dedicated repair function/cost. Score 1.

**F10 – Save/load:** serialize() → JSON via prompt(); loadBtn try/catches Game.deserialize(), alert(e.message) on bad input. Score 2.

**F11 – End conditions:** win (turn>=60,pop>=12,food/water>=50) and lose (pop===0) both reachable; computeScore() sums researchCount*20+turn*2+resourceSum (population term silently dropped by operator-precedence bug but 3 other value sources still contribute); endGameModal renders summary. Score 2.

**F12 – UI:** switchTab() wired to tabs and keydown 1-6; log entries show `Turn ${e.turn}`; tile-tooltip shows adjacency bonus text; Space ends turn; @media(max-width:600px) present. Score 2.

**F13 – Dev panel:** runTests() checks caps/negative resources/prereqs/seeded-determinism/save-load roundtrip (real invariants); runBenchmark() runs 200 turns headless, prints state hash via serialize(). Score 2.

**G1:** research.soil_enrichment/metallurgy/etc read directly in produceResources() output formula — solid link, but 4/12 techs (renewable_power, biotech, energy_storage, advanced_trading) never wired anywhere. Score 3.

**G2:** shortfall writes p.morale -=30 in endTurn(), but produceResources() never reads morale — labor output unaffected by morale. Score 1.

**G3:** triggerAshstorm() nulls buildings (produce 0 thereafter); rebuilding via build() spends resources and restores production — implemented as destroy+rebuild rather than damage-state+repair function. Score 2.

**G4:** caravan price formula uses only basePrice*random*tradeMultiplier; tradeMultiplier set by one event then reset, never reads stockpiles. Score 1.

**G5:** colonist_arrives choice pushes to population array; water_contamination choices differently mutate resources.water vs population morale — durable state writes via effect(g). Score 4.

